# Copy to .env and adjust per-machine, then run `direnv allow`.
# (Nothing here is a secret; .env is only gitignored so each machine can
# point at its own disk layout without touching tracked files.)

# Root directory for the shared Lake/Lean package+build cache (Mathlib
# clones alone run several GB). Lake has no env var that relocates
# .lake itself — LAKE_HOME only controls where Lake looks for its own
# binary install, not where it writes packages/build output — so the
# actual mechanism .envrc uses is a symlink: proofs/.lake ->
# $LEAN_CACHE_DIR/program-cheng-connectivity-asymptote-proofs. Point this
# at spare disk (an HDD, a second partition, etc.) instead of your root/home
# filesystem if that's tight on space.
LEAN_CACHE_DIR=/path/to/some/device/.lake
